      "side": 1,
      "message": "Comparing /proc/slabinfo before and after the change:\n\nbefore:\n# name            \u003cactive_objs\u003e \u003cnum_objs\u003e \u003cobjsize\u003e \u003cobjperslab\u003e \u003cpagesperslab\u003e : tunables \u003climit\u003e \u003cbatchcount\u003e \u003csharedfactor\u003e : slabdata \u003cactive_slabs\u003e \u003cnum_slabs\u003e \u003csharedavail\u003e\ntask_struct         3300   3591   4480    7    8 : tunables    0    0    0 : slabdata    521    521      0\n\nafter:\n# name            \u003cactive_objs\u003e \u003cnum_objs\u003e \u003cobjsize\u003e \u003cobjperslab\u003e \u003cpagesperslab\u003e : tunables \u003climit\u003e \u003cbatchcount\u003e \u003csharedfactor\u003e : slabdata \u003cactive_slabs\u003e \u003cnum_slabs\u003e \u003csharedavail\u003e\ntask_struct         3419   3647   4672    7    8 : tunables    0    0    0 : slabdata    521    521      0\n\nSo even though objsize increased from 4480 to 4672, the objperslab and pagesperslab are unchanged. So, effective memory consumption is unchanged.",
